{"repositoryId":1422656907,"availability":"available","full":"sequenzia/Interlock","name":"Interlock","description":"Runtime safety shield for a reinforcement learning agent. A decision model judges each action against plain-English operator rules, with a human on the loop.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-16T20:47:34Z","updated":"2026-10-17T05:38:10Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://interlock-sequenzia.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://interlock-sequenzia.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:54:02.581Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T18:54:02.581Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T18:54:02.581Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T18:54:02.581Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The policy was trained once. The rules changed live, in plain English.","Interlock is a runtime safety shield for a reinforcement learning agent, with a human on the loop. A Stable-Baselines3 DQN drives in highway-env on task reward alone and knows nothing about rules. At every step, Jev, TypeSafe's decision model, judges each of the agent's candidate actions against operator rules typed in plain English and returns a probability of violation. Code then allows the action, falls back to the agent's next-best safe action, or pauses and asks a human. An operator console shows the road, the rules, the approval queue, a decision inspector and the evaluation numbers.","Built as a demo of runtime safety for learned policies and human-on-the-loop design."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sequenzia/Interlock/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"24e104c09e4a37ca250e439e0775c267d606c9658e394daf112020396efc53e5","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T18:54:02.692Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:54:02.692Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The policy was trained once. The rules changed live, in plain English.","sourceUrl":"